      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786683345921,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "**** Metrics ingestion ****",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "**** Metrics ingestion ****",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Yj4jO5mYMPrdsh1o5odQr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1187.8625989477118,
      "y": 1053.3602897246647,
      "width": 482.13970947265625,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b22",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1847780744,
      "version": 151,
      "versionNonce": 643319232,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786683611106,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Query and visualize metrics on dashboard ***\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Query and visualize metrics on dashboard ***\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "G3ICjYnN0MehKx2ykcLh7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1190.4505025518893,
      "y": 897.412150041881,
      "width": 983.559326171875,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b26",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1497512952,
      "version": 1310,
      "versionNonce": 903531968,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786683618314,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- Storage layer: dashboard queries are demanding. (eg: p99 over x hours, etc, with filtering...)\n-- Using relational DB can work for small dataset, but can cause bottleneck over time \n-- Time-Series database (InfluxDB, TimescaleDB)\n\n1) Append only write: data is written in time series order and never update (almost).\nThis would allow LSM tree or append only storage engine achieve high write throughput\n2) Time-based partitioning: data is chunk by time, so queries for time series only touch\na specific chunk. Others could drop without impact the current window\n3) Columnar compression: timestamp + values compressed when stored together\n(eg: CPU metrics in one host compress from 100k to 5k)\n4) Built-in rollups/down sampling: database can compute 1-m, 1-hour, etc... aggregation automatically. \n===> fast long-range queries\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- Storage layer: dashboard queries are demanding. (eg: p99 over x hours, etc, with filtering...)\n-- Using relational DB can work for small dataset, but can cause bottleneck over time \n-- Time-Series database (InfluxDB, TimescaleDB)\n\n1) Append only write: data is written in time series order and never update (almost).\nThis would allow LSM tree or append only storage engine achieve high write throughput\n2) Time-based partitioning: data is chunk by time, so queries for time series only touch\na specific chunk. Others could drop without impact the current window\n3) Columnar compression: timestamp + values compressed when stored together\n(eg: CPU metrics in one host compress from 100k to 5k)\n4) Built-in rollups/down sampling: database can compute 1-m, 1-hour, etc... aggregation automatically. \n===> fast long-range queries\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "gh2LeNPA_yzf_w-rl2SAT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1190.4641818777784,
      "y": 1215.0795011267062,
      "width": 895.3193359375,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b27",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1535675896,
      "version": 210,
      "versionNonce": 1445459392,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786683632678,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "==> Time-series databases struggle with high-cardinality data - \nmillions of unique label combinations create millions of series, and each series has overhead. \nWe'll need cardinality controls to prevent runaway growth.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "==> Time-series databases struggle with high-cardinality data - \nmillions of unique label combinations create millions of series, and each series has overhead. \nWe'll need cardinality controls to prevent runaway growth.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
