      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bNVFhU8EZO4OelgH_1FVf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1181.0929106543335,
      "y": 2461.257332992193,
      "width": 1021.4392700195312,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1196375370,
      "version": 319,
      "versionNonce": 864585152,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786683952408,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nThe flow looks like:\n1. Data point arrives at ingestion service\n2. Strip any label keys not in the allowlist\n3. Hash the remaining labels to get a series ID\n4. Check Redis to see if this series already exists\n5. If new, check against the per-metric series cap\n6. If under cap, accept and publish to Kafka; if over cap, drop and increment a dropped_metrics counter.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nThe flow looks like:\n1. Data point arrives at ingestion service\n2. Strip any label keys not in the allowlist\n3. Hash the remaining labels to get a series ID\n4. Check Redis to see if this series already exists\n5. If new, check against the per-metric series cap\n6. If under cap, accept and publish to Kafka; if over cap, drop and increment a dropped_metrics counter.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
